# CODEOWNERS
#
# These owners are automatically requested for review when someone opens a
# pull request that modifies files matching the patterns below.
#
# Format: pattern    @owner
# Docs: https://docs.github.com/en/repositories/managing-your-repositorys-settings-and-features/customizing-your-repository/about-code-owners

# Default: all files require review from the founding team
*                                           @your-org/core

# Algorithm — any change to pruning logic requires a second reviewer
src/pruner/                                 @your-org/core @your-org/algorithm-reviewers
docs/ALGORITHM.md                           @your-org/core

# Billing — requires two reviewers, no exceptions
src/billing/                                @your-org/core @your-org/billing-reviewers
supabase/migrations/                        @your-org/core

# Security-critical — TEE, crypto, and ZK-Context
src/proxy/tee/                              @your-org/core @your-org/security-reviewers
src/pruner/crypto.ts                        @your-org/core @your-org/security-reviewers
docs/SECURITY.md                            @your-org/core @your-org/security-reviewers
docs/enclave-pcr-values.md                  @your-org/core @your-org/security-reviewers
SECURITY_POLICY.md                          @your-org/core

# Architecture decisions — founder must approve all ADRs
docs/decisions/                             @your-org/core

# Eval framework — any threshold change requires explicit approval
docs/EVAL_FRAMEWORK.md                      @your-org/core
evals/                                      @your-org/core

# Claude Code instructions — changes here affect all AI-assisted development
.claude/CLAUDE.md                           @your-org/core

# Documentation — any contributor can update docs but core reviews
docs/                                       @your-org/core
README.md                                   @your-org/core
CONTRIBUTING.md                             @your-org/core
CHANGELOG.md                                @your-org/core
